# SFT execution status v0.100

2026-09-21. The approved one-shot SDK capacity preflight was published and
executed once. It **failed before deletion** at the bounded metadata census.
Gate 5 and the capacity blocker remain open. No GPU, image acquisition, model
or dataset access, native qualification, or training occurred.

## Published scope and validation

Commit `7d6007defa8868c4276372411b7ae6ca1189ec75` adds exactly four files: the
new cleanup script, synthetic tests, one-shot workflow, and versioned plan.
Parent `716774386cc3eba22f860c7699d6a33654882a02` and the private repository
identity were checked before the non-force push. No prior tracked file changed.

The 54 new tests plus 93 frozen regressions pass on both CPython 3.11.15 and
3.13.7. Ruff 0.15.1 finds no new E/F/I/B/UP findings. Independent review found no
blocking scope issue under the explicitly stated trusted disposable VM and
no-concurrent-writers premise. The original 16 GiB floor remains unchanged.

## Actual result, not a successful cleanup

[Fresh run 35616015735](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/35616015735)
used attempt 1 and job `106386798089`, lasting 49 seconds including setup and
artifact upload. Hash authentication and the synthetic test step succeeded.
The exact-target cleanup step failed with `stage=census`, `code=budget_exhausted`.

The authenticated 928-byte aggregate confirms `removal_started=false`, zero
removed leaves/directories, no SDK root removal, and no setup-probe execution.
The Mac SDK and other real local resources were not touched; local deletion
tests operated only on their own synthetic temporary fixtures.

Available disk before the census was 14,347,677,696 bytes; the unchanged
theoretical pre-acquisition requirement was 18,241,982,464 bytes. There is no
after-cleanup measurement because no cleanup started.

The `census_nodes=0` and `census_allocated_bytes=0` fields are **unpopulated
defaults**, not evidence of an empty SDK. The script only publishes those fields
after the census returns. Its coarse code does not distinguish listing/global
node count, directory depth, cumulative relative-name bytes, or allocated block
bytes. This is a definite diagnostic limitation; neither the crossed limit nor
a traversal bug is established by the result. Do not guess actual SDK size.

Artifact `10645608530` is a 623-byte ZIP with server digest
`e793b925aa1f90f1d0fb9c7d681452242a0bd1b4dd58c840d500bd2dc101e757`.
Only its single canonical aggregate was retained; no raw logs or ZIP were saved.
The aggregate SHA-256 is
`4b26a0457ca9e81a043fc8d77ebb4b301e5101898c0e9917d25173b59cf7939e`.
Two zero-network structural verification passes succeeded. Prior bound evidence
and frozen native sources remain byte-for-byte unchanged.

## CI and remaining boundary

Spark source checks succeeded. Source CI's lint, isolated controls, and
source-only validators succeeded; the remaining source-suite job is still
running at this note's initial recording. Its final result will be recorded
separately once observed. The preflight failure must remain visible, not be
deleted or mislabeled as a pass.

The approved attempt is consumed and was not retried. No limits were raised and
no broader deletion was attempted. The next justified scope is one separately
approved, fresh, read-only same-target metadata census with budget-specific
codes and bounded partial counters, retaining the existing caps. It must not
delete SDK entries, acquire software/model objects, or run qualification.
Only its result can justify a specific later correction; it does not authorize
another cleanup. `production_eligible=false` remains unchanged.

